.TH DDN-FETCH "1" "2026\-11\-19" "ddnetmirror 0.0.1" "ddnetmirror manual"
.SH NAME
ddn fetch \- fetch running configs, LLDP links and a Containerlab topology from CloudVision
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ddn
fetch [-h] --server SERVER (--hostname HOSTNAME | --tag KEY=VALUE) [--ca-file CA_FILE] [--output OUTPUT | --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR] [--lldp] [--lab-name LAB_NAME] [--image IMAGE] [--fixup-rules RULES.yml] [--verbose] [--force]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetch running configs from CloudVision and save them unchanged. The service\-account token is read from CLOUDVISION_TOKEN, or else from $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ddnetmirror/token (default ~/.config/ddnetmirror/token).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI\,SERVER\/\fR
CloudVision host[:port] (default port 443)

.TP
\fB\-\-hostname\fR \fI\,HOSTNAME\/\fR
device hostname as shown in CloudVision inventory (any case)

.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI\,KEY=VALUE\/\fR
device tag; must match exactly one device unless \-\-output\-dir is given

.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-file\fR \fI\,CA_FILE\/\fR
PEM CA bundle for on\-prem CVP with a private CA

.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,OUTPUT\/\fR
output file (default: <device hostname>.cfg); never overwritten

.TP
\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fI\,OUTPUT_DIR\/\fR
with \-\-tag: collect every device with the tag into DIR as <hostname>.cfg

.TP
\fB\-\-lldp\fR
with \-\-output\-dir: also report LLDP links between the collected devices

.TP
\fB\-\-lab\-name\fR \fI\,LAB_NAME\/\fR
with \-\-lldp: also write a Containerlab topology DIR/<NAME>.clab.yml

.TP
\fB\-\-image\fR \fI\,IMAGE\/\fR
with \-\-lab\-name: cEOS image for every topology node, no Docker check. Without
it, a local ceos:VERSION image is picked per device by EOS version (needs
Docker; version matching only, not a compatibility check)

.TP
\fB\-\-fixup\-rules\fR \fI\,RULES.yml\/\fR
with \-\-lab\-name: keep originals in DIR/collected, write copies transformed by
these rules to DIR/startup, and use those as startup configs

.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
with \-\-fixup\-rules: print what each rule changed per device; never prints
config text

.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
with \-\-output\-dir: replace existing generated files (collected and startup
configs, topology) instead of refusing; no backups, other files untouched

.SH DISTRIBUTION
The latest version of ddnetmirror may be downloaded from
.UR https://github.com/DaphnisDuck/ddnetmirror
.UE
